---

## 🎯 Quick Checklist Before Launch

- ✅ All core pages render correctly on mobile, tablet, desktop.  
- ✅ Lighthouse score ≥ 90 (performance, accessibility, best practices).  
- ✅ All forms validate client‑side and server‑side.  
- ✅ Cart persists across sessions (localStorage or cookie).  
- ✅ Payment flow tested with Stripe test keys.  
- ✅ Admin routes protected (JWT + role checks).  
- ✅ CI pipeline passes lint, tests, build.  
- ✅ Deployment to Vercel with preview URLs.  
- ✅ Error tracking (Sentry) and analytics (GA4) integrated.  

---

### Final Thought

Building a robust e‑commerce frontend is a marathon, not a sprint. Start with a solid foundation (Next.js + Tailwind + Redux Toolkit), iterate quickly with a well‑defined backlog, and keep performance, accessibility, and security at the forefront. Once you’re comfortable with the core, you can layer in advanced features like progressive web app (PWA) support, server‑less functions for heavy computations, or even AI‑powered recommendations.

Happy coding! 🚀
